<Layout title="About · NZ GIS History"><div class="wrap narrative"><p class="eyebrow">About the publication</p><h1>A History of GIS in New Zealand</h1><p>This publication brings together historical accounts, people, organisations, projects, events and sources. Its connected entries provide routes through the material alongside sequential reading.</p><p>Dates retain their recorded precision. Links identify mentions, thematic associations or documented relationships according to their evidence. A linked event does not automatically establish a date in a person's biography.</p><p><a href="/stories/preface/">Read the author's preface</a> for the background to the project.</p><h2>Sources and images</h2><p>Sources appear beside passages, entries and events. Image details retain attribution and licence information. Historical images are used where the available permissions allow reproduction.</p><p><a href="/images/">Image register</a> · <a href="/release.json">Publication revision</a> · <a href="https://github.com/pm4gis/gishistory26">Project repository</a></p></div></Layout>
